Use in Retail
Computer vision solutions like CNN-based image classification model can be widely used for automation, quality control, 
customer analytics, and operational efficiency.
This detects visual patterns from images, which is very useful in retail environments.
This can help retailers automate product inspection, inventory monitoring, customer analytics, and smart checkout systems 
by using CNNs to recognize products, defects, and visual patterns from images
Use in Manufacturing
Computer vision solutions like CNN-based defect detection model are extremely useful in the manufacturing domain because 
they can automatically inspect products and detect defects from images in real time.
In manufacturing, this computer vision solution can automatically inspect products, detect defects such as scratches or dents, 
improve quality control, reduce manual inspection, and increase production efficiency using CNN-based image analysis.
Use in Healthcare
Computer vision solutions like CNN-based image classification are widely used in healthcare to analyze medical images 
and assist doctors in diagnosis, detection, and monitoring of diseases.
In healthcare, this type of computer vision solution can analyze medical images to detect diseases, tumors, abnormalities, 
and other health conditions automatically using CNN-based image classification and pattern recognition
Use in Agriculture
Computer vision solutions like CNN-based image classification are widely used in agriculture to monitor crops, detect diseases,
improve productivity, and automate farming tasks.
In agriculture, this type of computer vision solution can detect plant diseases, monitor crop health, identify pests, 
inspect produce quality, and automate farming operations using CNN-based image analysis.
Use in Security
Computer vision solutions like CNN-based image classification are widely used in security and surveillance systems to 
automatically detect threats, recognize people or objects, and monitor suspicious activities from images or video feeds.
In security, this type of computer vision solution can automatically detect faces, intrusions, suspicious activities, 
weapons, and threats from images or surveillance footage using CNN-based image analysis and pattern recognition.
Use in Autonomus vehicles
Computer vision solutions like CNN-based image classification are one of the core technologies used in autonomous vehicles 
(self-driving cars) to help vehicles understand their surroundings and make driving decisions automatically.
In autonomous vehicles, this type of computer vision solution helps detect roads, vehicles, pedestrians, traffic signs,
and obstacles so the vehicle can navigate and drive safely using CNN-based image analysis.
